    {
      "layer": "military_security",
      "tag": "muscovite_expansion_pressure",
      "direction": "decline",
      "description": "The expansion of the Russian state progressively closed the steppe frontier: the construction of defensive lines (zasechnaya cherta) restricted Tatar raiding, and Ivan the Terrible's capture of Kazan (1552) and Astrakhan (1556) isolated Crimea from eastern Tatar allies.",
      "sources": [
